cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PSI in research, please cite the relevant Zenodo record when available and this repository for the evolving public source."
title: "PSI: Identifiability under constrained observation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Smoczynski"
    given-names: "Bartek"
repository-code: "https://github.com/smoczynski-b/PSI"
url: "https://omni-artificial-intelligence-lab-sc4ilj.v2.appdeploy.ai/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  PSI is a formal research framework for justified inference under constrained
  observation. It studies compatible fibers, task-relative identifiability,
  separating tests, representation sufficiency, provenance and controlled
  decision procedures for human and AI reasoning.
keywords:
  - identifiability
  - inference
  - artificial intelligence
  - uncertainty
  - observation
  - verification
